---
import Button from '../ui/Button.astro';
---

<div class="why-build-copy editorial-content">
  <p>
    I started building for the web because I wanted to make things people actually use.
    Not templates — products. Dashboards that surface the right data, workflows that cut real friction,
    interfaces that feel considered instead of cobbled together.
  </p>
  <p>
    Working across 5+ client platforms at Martinrea shifted my thinking from "write code" to "ship outcomes."
    Every replatforming project taught me the same lesson: the architecture decisions you make on day one
    echo through every sprint after it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Today I focus on React and TypeScript SaaS products — full-stack, design-aware, and built to scale
    without becoming painful to maintain. If it ships, it should ship right.
  </p>
  <nav class="why-build-ctas" aria-label="About page shortcuts">
    <Button href="/skills" variant="primary">
      My Experience <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
    </Button>
    <Button href="/projects" variant="secondary">
      Things I've Built <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
    </Button>
  </nav>
</div>

<style>
  .why-build-copy {
    gap: 0.95rem;
  }

  .why-build-copy p {
    max-width: none;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .why-build-ctas {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
  }
</style>
